04:50.005 --> 04:52.758
-This isn't bad!
-Yeah!

04:52.925 --> 04:56.345
-I feel like having a beer.
-Yeah.

04:56.512 --> 04:58.805
At least wait until tonight!

05:00.015 --> 05:02.559
-An oncoming car.
-This is bad. Hide!

05:10.692 --> 05:12.194
Great! No problem.

05:12.361 --> 05:15.447
It didn't look like anyone was riding back here.

05:15.614 --> 05:19.368
It just looked like a normal truck carrying a few corpses.

05:20.452 --> 05:22.371
What are you doing?

05:22.871 --> 05:24.873
What are they doing?

05:25.666 --> 05:29.378
All right. Pick something you'd like to eat.

05:29.586 --> 05:32.005
When we get back, let's each make a dish!

05:32.172 --> 05:33.757
Oh, nice idea.

05:33.966 --> 05:36.760
-All right. Good luck!
-Yeah!

05:45.477 --> 05:47.563
Lalako-tan!

05:47.771 --> 05:50.065
There's lots of unusual things here.

05:51.233 --> 05:53.944
It tests our ability to choose ingredients.

05:54.111 --> 05:57.114
I wonder what the guys are going to choose.

05:57.281 --> 05:58.282
Are you okay?

05:58.448 --> 06:01.076
Yeah. I'll go ask them.

06:01.285 --> 06:02.786
Welcome! What would you like?

06:02.953 --> 06:05.581
-Oh, there you are.
-I...

06:06.373 --> 06:09.084
want to eat an old man.

06:11.878 --> 06:13.422
What's wrong, Cakey?

06:13.589 --> 06:14.673
What happened?

06:14.840 --> 06:16.842
Azusa...

06:17.050 --> 06:19.886
was trying to eat the old man at the fish stall.

06:20.053 --> 06:21.430
An old man at a fish stall?

06:21.597 --> 06:23.599
What did you see?

06:24.725 --> 06:26.893
I probably just heard wrong.

06:27.060 --> 06:28.270
Really?

06:28.437 --> 06:30.105
Then that's good.

06:32.316 --> 06:34.776
-I'm going to ask Tokita.
-Okay.

06:34.943 --> 06:37.112
I don't get what's going on. Just go.

06:37.529 --> 06:40.365
-Um...
-Oh, I see. I...

06:40.866 --> 06:42.451
want Hamasaki's wife.

06:45.329 --> 06:48.206
-Aina?
-Tokita...

06:48.373 --> 06:49.875
What about him?

06:50.709 --> 06:53.712
-Tokita was trying to get with a married woman.
-Hold on.

06:53.879 --> 06:55.881
What did you hear just now?

06:56.340 --> 06:58.383
Maybe you heard wrong.

06:58.550 --> 07:00.302
I heard it clearly!

07:00.469 --> 07:02.095
You must be hearing things.

07:02.262 --> 07:04.222
Then let's go and find out together.

07:04.389 --> 07:05.474
I don't mind.

07:05.641 --> 07:07.017
Oh, dear.

07:09.478 --> 07:11.897
Welcome! What are you looking for?

07:12.272 --> 07:13.899
He's just shopping like normal.

07:14.066 --> 07:16.151
There's nothing weird going on.

07:16.318 --> 07:17.861
You think so?

07:18.028 --> 07:20.113
You must have misunderstood, Aina.

07:20.280 --> 07:23.909
They wouldn't do anything weird in a place like this.

07:24.201 --> 07:25.410
You're right.

07:25.577 --> 07:29.414
-We have everything. Just tell me what you're looking for.
-All right.

07:29.706 --> 07:31.416
A chubby high school student.

07:31.583 --> 07:32.918
Out!

07:33.210 --> 07:34.961
What's he trying to buy here?

07:35.128 --> 07:36.672
I told you!

07:36.838 --> 07:38.340
Should we turn him in?

07:38.507 --> 07:41.009
We should talk to him first.

07:41.176 --> 07:42.511
Wait, you two.

07:43.053 --> 07:45.639
-I think you guys have the wrong idea.
-What?

07:47.140 --> 07:49.685
Those are all names of fish.

07:49.893 --> 07:52.521
-Really?
-What amazing names!

07:52.688 --> 07:55.232
Then what Azusa and Tokita said just now...

07:55.399 --> 07:58.235
-They were trying to buy fish?
-Yeah.

07:58.402 --> 08:01.405
Of course, they wouldn't actually
try to buy stuff like that.

08:01.571 --> 08:04.700
Well... I knew what was going on all along.

08:04.908 --> 08:07.369
You were surprised too.

08:07.536 --> 08:09.955
-Excuse me.
-Hi, welcome.

08:10.163 --> 08:13.417
I need a poisonous fish
that can knock an adult out with one bite.

08:13.583 --> 08:15.127
We don't sell things like that here.

08:18.171 --> 08:20.674
It's not nice spying on people while they shop!

08:20.841 --> 08:23.552
You're the one who was trying to buy a poisonous fish!

08:23.719 --> 08:26.471
You're planning something weird again!

08:26.680 --> 08:29.975
It didn't work. If I don't do something...

08:31.268 --> 08:33.979
I'm going to end up dying of embarrassment!

08:34.146 --> 08:36.189
Okay, everybody draw one.

08:37.065 --> 08:38.275
What for?

08:38.442 --> 08:41.236
It's to decide who cooks first.

08:41.403 --> 08:43.613
We won't all fit in the kitchen.

08:43.780 --> 08:47.242
-We're going to take turns cooking in pairs.
-That's why.

08:47.409 --> 08:49.536
I just have to draw one, right?

08:50.162 --> 08:51.621
Cooking in pairs?

08:52.247 --> 08:55.625
That means if I can get Kohei paired up with Cakey...

08:56.126 --> 08:59.212
I can practice while they're cooking!

09:00.380 --> 09:02.507
-I'm number four.
-I'm number two.

09:02.674 --> 09:06.511
Please pair me up with Chisa.
Please pair me up with Chisa.

09:06.678 --> 09:09.639
Please pair me up with Chisa.
Please pair me up with Chisa.

09:09.973 --> 09:12.893
-Iori?
-Please, God!

09:13.059 --> 09:14.060
Please!

09:15.353 --> 09:17.397
Yeah!

09:17.689 --> 09:19.858
Hey, Chisa! We're paired up!

09:20.025 --> 09:22.819
Aina, That guy is gross. Can you switch with me?

09:22.986 --> 09:24.905
Why are you saying that, Chisa?

09:25.197 --> 09:28.533
We'll have fun cooking together as a pair!

09:28.700 --> 09:31.077
-He is gross.
-What are you going to do?

09:31.244 --> 09:33.789
I'm going to hold onto the knife the whole time.

09:33.955 --> 09:36.416
Iori, you went overboard.

09:37.876 --> 09:39.127
What do you mean?

09:39.294 --> 09:41.671
No way. Did Azusa notice?

09:41.838 --> 09:43.632
You went overboard with everything.

09:44.132 --> 09:47.636
You're trying to make Kohei jealous, right?

09:49.596 --> 09:51.389
Yeah!

09:53.934 --> 09:56.937
Is that good? You're crying?

09:57.103 --> 09:59.689
It's our turn to cook.

10:00.899 --> 10:02.692
Why are you so far away?

10:04.903 --> 10:08.198
Even if I practice, it's hard doing it on my own.

10:09.241 --> 10:12.452
Should I tell her what's going on and ask her to help?

10:12.744 --> 10:13.829
Hey, Chisa.

10:14.955 --> 10:16.498
-What?
-Actually...

10:18.416 --> 10:20.085
I'll get some tea.

10:20.293 --> 10:22.045
That's the issue.

10:22.212 --> 10:23.839
So that's what's going on.

10:24.005 --> 10:26.591
So, Chisa, to help me practice...

10:27.217 --> 10:28.593
will you go out with me?

10:30.804 --> 10:35.100
What's going on? Why did Iori just ask Chisa that?

10:35.267 --> 10:39.229
Calm down. I might have gotten the wrong idea,
just like when we were shopping.

10:39.396 --> 10:42.357
-Are you serious?
-Yeah. I'm serious.

10:42.941 --> 10:46.361
-I've fallen in love.
-I don't have the wrong idea!

10:46.528 --> 10:47.529
But, Chisa...

10:47.696 --> 10:51.116
You said you could never imagine dating him...

10:51.491 --> 10:54.619
-Really? I'm glad.
-No!

10:55.036 --> 10:58.623
-Are you sure you're okay with me?
-Yeah. You're the only one.

10:59.708 --> 11:01.668
What's wrong, Cakey?

11:01.835 --> 11:04.629
-Chisa and Iori...
-What happened to them?

11:05.130 --> 11:08.008
She was against it until just a few days ago!

11:08.174 --> 11:09.634
What are you talking about?

11:09.801 --> 11:12.053
I don't want to talk about it.

11:12.220 --> 11:15.140
I bet you just have the wrong idea again.

11:15.307 --> 11:19.227
If you don't have any weights, you'll float.
It'll be hard to practice.

11:19.394 --> 11:22.397
Then we can just put heavy things on me.

11:22.564 --> 11:24.608
Can you tie me up?

11:25.400 --> 11:29.154
What's going on? Is what Cakey said just now true?

11:29.321 --> 11:32.157
Was she talking about the awakening of a sexual fetish?

11:32.324 --> 11:34.951
No. I can't tell from just that one sentence.

11:35.118 --> 11:36.953
That's kind of dangerous.

11:37.120 --> 11:39.289
I see. Then can you at least...

11:39.456 --> 11:41.166
I have to confirm the truth!

11:41.333 --> 11:43.627
...step on me with all your strength?

11:46.880 --> 11:48.048
How was it?

11:48.214 --> 11:50.133
You're right...

11:50.300 --> 11:52.802
I never imagined he'd awaken...

11:52.969 --> 11:55.639
I see. So he did awaken.

11:55.805 --> 11:57.140
I'm back!

11:57.307 --> 11:59.893
-Welcome back.
-Sorry I'm late.

12:00.060 --> 12:02.604
-Is dinner okay?
-No problem.

12:02.771 --> 12:06.650
-It's our turn now.
-I'm glad I'm on time.

12:06.816 --> 12:09.527
Dinner is fine, but...

12:16.117 --> 12:20.080
For some reason,
Iori and the others are acting strange.

12:20.246 --> 12:22.874
-Iori?
-What did you do?

12:23.041 --> 12:24.876
Nothing in particular.

12:44.062 --> 12:45.313
Chisa?

12:47.232 --> 12:50.485
Sorry to ask you to come.

12:50.735 --> 12:52.821
That's Iori's voice.

12:53.196 --> 12:57.325
What if--? Are they trying to sneak in
some alone time since they're dating now?

12:57.909 --> 12:59.369
I'm going to get wet.

12:59.536 --> 13:02.080
You should take off your clothes.

13:02.330 --> 13:04.791
Okay, I'm taking my clothes off.

13:04.958 --> 13:08.586
-Okay. Let's do it.
-What?

13:08.837 --> 13:10.588
What are you doing?

13:13.717 --> 13:16.511
What are you doing?

13:17.721 --> 13:19.556
Cakey! What are you doing here?

13:19.723 --> 13:21.558
That's what I was about to say!

13:21.725 --> 13:25.103
You were acting weird. Now you're doing weird things!

13:25.270 --> 13:28.398
This is-- I dropped my wallet in the pool.

13:28.565 --> 13:30.108
Liar!

13:30.316 --> 13:32.861
Iori, tell me the truth.

13:33.028 --> 13:35.613
You've been hiding something since yesterday, right?

13:36.865 --> 13:39.117
It's no use. I'll tell you the truth.

13:39.743 --> 13:41.202
-Cakey...
-Yeah?

13:41.369 --> 13:43.538
We're practicing diving.

13:43.705 --> 13:46.207
Why won't you tell me the truth?

13:46.374 --> 13:48.293
I did tell you the truth!

13:48.460 --> 13:52.047
You're engaged in some sort of advanced adult activity!

13:52.464 --> 13:54.758
No, this is for beginners.

13:55.008 --> 13:58.762
Aina, we really are practicing diving.

13:59.512 --> 14:02.766
-Really?
-Why do you believe it when Chisa says it?

14:03.767 --> 14:06.269
We were practicing mask clearing.

14:06.478 --> 14:08.146
I see.

14:08.354 --> 14:10.732
Then you should have told me earlier.

14:10.899 --> 14:13.193
I didn't want you to laugh at me.

14:13.359 --> 14:16.738
I wouldn't laugh at you!
I would've helped you if you had told me.

14:16.905 --> 14:19.032
-Really?
-That'd be a big help.

14:19.282 --> 14:20.867
So, what should I do?

14:21.034 --> 14:22.535
Oh, well, then...

14:30.794 --> 14:33.546
-Don't struggle!
-Stop kicking!

14:33.713 --> 14:35.048
Hello. Is this the police?

14:37.175 --> 14:39.427
There's still water in my mask.

14:39.677 --> 14:42.013
You're almost there.

14:42.180 --> 14:44.349
Maybe you're still afraid of the water.

14:44.516 --> 14:46.434
It's come down to this. Let's do it.

14:46.684 --> 14:48.436
It?

14:48.853 --> 14:51.523
Yeah. We did it before.

14:52.816 --> 14:54.818
I'm in a bathtub.

14:54.984 --> 14:56.277
I'm in a bathtub.

14:56.444 --> 14:59.322
-You did this before?
-I had nothing to do with it.

14:59.489 --> 15:01.783
Does that really work?

15:01.950 --> 15:04.410
-No. It didn't work at all.
-What?

15:04.577 --> 15:06.204
Then why are you doing it?

15:11.167 --> 15:12.293
I thought...

15:12.460 --> 15:15.547
I'd be able to get closer here.

15:16.881 --> 15:19.926
I want to do everything I can.

15:21.636 --> 15:23.888
Anyway, you can go to sleep.

15:24.055 --> 15:26.933
-Okay.
-Don't overdo it.

15:27.100 --> 15:28.977
Thanks for coming.

15:29.144 --> 15:30.854
-Goodnight.
-Goodnight.

15:31.020 --> 15:32.939
Yeah, good night.

15:34.691 --> 15:35.984
Well, then...

15:45.326 --> 15:47.745
All right. Not bad.

15:47.912 --> 15:49.414
Excuse me.

15:50.790 --> 15:52.500
I'm from the police.

15:54.085 --> 15:57.297
Someone reported a girl and a guy
engaging in unusual behavior.

15:57.463 --> 16:00.383
Well... I think there's been a mistake.

16:00.550 --> 16:04.012
I didn't see anyone suspicious.

16:04.220 --> 16:05.763
-Oh, really?
-Yes.

16:05.930 --> 16:09.517
I didn't see any dangerous people like that.

16:10.101 --> 16:14.522
Just in case, I'm going to look around
to make sure there's no one suspicious here.

16:15.648 --> 16:17.025
I understand.

16:20.987 --> 16:23.281
I can't get out.

16:33.499 --> 16:36.294
You're saying Iori's in bed because he caught a cold?

16:36.502 --> 16:37.629
That's right.

16:37.795 --> 16:40.215
When I woke up, his face was red.

16:40.381 --> 16:41.549
I was surprised.

16:42.508 --> 16:47.430
-Iori's always like that!
-Even the way idiots get sick is different.

16:47.639 --> 16:51.142
His fever isn't that high, so I think he'll be okay.

16:51.309 --> 16:53.436
He can't participate in today's lessons.

16:53.603 --> 16:55.939
It's because of what I said.

16:56.105 --> 16:59.442
No, it's not your fault.

16:59.609 --> 17:02.946
This is obviously his own fault.

17:03.112 --> 17:04.906
Anyway...

17:05.073 --> 17:07.033
Let's let Iori sleep.

17:07.200 --> 17:10.828
Aina and Kohei have to concentrate
on getting their licenses.

17:10.995 --> 17:12.956
-Yes!
-Okay.

17:22.173 --> 17:24.467
I feel better after sleeping.

17:27.303 --> 17:30.223
Oh, you look like you're feeling better, Iori.

17:30.390 --> 17:33.268
Azusa, you didn't go diving?

17:33.476 --> 17:36.062
-Yeah.
-Sorry. It's my fault.

17:36.229 --> 17:37.855
What are you talking about?

17:38.022 --> 17:39.983
So, how are you feeling?

17:40.149 --> 17:41.859
I'm feeling much better.

17:42.026 --> 17:44.487
It'd be best if you took some medicine,

17:44.654 --> 17:46.531
but the pharmacy isn't open.

17:46.698 --> 17:48.074
There's no need for that.

17:48.241 --> 17:49.617
No, Iori!

17:50.493 --> 17:52.287
You're going in the ocean tomorrow.

17:52.453 --> 17:53.997
So, you have to fully recover.

17:54.747 --> 17:56.666
They didn't have any medicine,

17:56.833 --> 17:58.584
but they had this.

18:03.798 --> 18:06.342
Azusa, what's that?

18:06.509 --> 18:08.636
A famous home remedy. You don't know it?

18:08.803 --> 18:10.722
I know. I do know.

18:10.888 --> 18:12.265
The only problem is...

18:12.432 --> 18:13.599
Is it number 1 or 2?

18:14.142 --> 18:15.852
All right, Iori.

18:16.853 --> 18:17.895
Yes?

18:18.062 --> 18:20.064
Stick out your neck.

18:21.065 --> 18:22.942
Good, it's number 1!

18:23.109 --> 18:26.112
-What's wrong?
-Nothing.

18:28.072 --> 18:31.617
-Here. Okay.
-Thank you.

18:31.784 --> 18:33.661
ANOTHER ONE

18:33.828 --> 18:35.913
Can you pull down your pants next?

18:36.080 --> 18:38.166
No, a combination technique!

18:39.125 --> 18:41.127
Azusa, you don't have to do this for me!

18:41.294 --> 18:43.421
No, no. There's no medicine.

18:43.588 --> 18:44.922
So we have to do this.

18:45.632 --> 18:47.925
No. If I don't do something,

18:48.426 --> 18:51.429
something else other than my health
is going to be destroyed!

18:53.306 --> 18:55.933
I'm going to look for some other medicine!

18:58.144 --> 19:01.147
This is perfect for medicine, right?

19:01.314 --> 19:04.525
True. It disinfects, stimulates perspiration,
and induces sleep.

19:04.692 --> 19:06.444
It's also rich in nutrients.

19:08.154 --> 19:09.947
It's the best medicine!

19:10.114 --> 19:12.950
Sick people shouldn't drink it though.

19:13.159 --> 19:16.954
But, if I drink now and fall sleep,
I won't be able to sleep at night.

19:17.163 --> 19:19.957
You haven't been able to sleep at night anyway.

19:20.124 --> 19:22.418
That's for a different reason.

19:22.585 --> 19:23.836
A different reason?

19:24.003 --> 19:25.380
You know...

19:25.546 --> 19:28.132
I feel nervous sleeping next to you and Nanaka,

19:28.299 --> 19:30.593
so I can't fall asleep.

19:30.760 --> 19:32.637
Oh, I didn't know that.

19:32.804 --> 19:35.807
Sorry about that.

19:37.183 --> 19:38.351
Azusa?

19:38.518 --> 19:40.812
-Hey, Iori.
-Yes?

19:41.938 --> 19:43.314
Do you want to have sex?

19:47.735 --> 19:50.738
-What are you saying!?
-You won't be nervous anymore, right?

19:50.905 --> 19:53.699
No! It's not something to do so casually!

19:54.283 --> 19:55.576
That's so rude.

19:55.827 --> 19:58.746
I don't do it with just any guy.

20:00.706 --> 20:03.376
But I do like you.

20:03.626 --> 20:05.294
I'm fine with doing it once.

20:05.461 --> 20:07.505
She's acting like it's a sport!

20:07.713 --> 20:10.007
I'm half joking.

20:10.174 --> 20:12.552
It'd be bad if things got awkward between us.

20:12.719 --> 20:14.262
Half?

20:14.804 --> 20:17.765
Yeah. Half.

20:18.766 --> 20:22.270
If you seriously want to do it, I'm okay with that.

20:27.525 --> 20:28.776
I'm being tested!

20:29.527 --> 20:30.528
I'm...

20:31.195 --> 20:32.280
really...

20:32.488 --> 20:34.282
being tested right now!

20:36.826 --> 20:38.286
I'm...

20:38.494 --> 20:40.329
going to say no.

20:41.748 --> 20:43.291
That's too bad.

20:46.043 --> 20:47.753
By the way, Azusa...

20:48.713 --> 20:51.883
You like Tokita as well as Nanaka, right?

20:52.049 --> 20:53.050
That's right.

20:53.259 --> 20:56.554
Why don't you go after Tokita?

20:58.473 --> 21:01.225
Tokki is kind of, you know...

21:01.392 --> 21:03.144
I'd be wasting my time chasing him.

21:03.311 --> 21:05.563
So it's different with Nanaka?

21:05.980 --> 21:07.648
A waste of time? Why?

21:07.815 --> 21:09.942
Don't you know, Iori?

21:10.109 --> 21:13.321
-What?
-Tokki, you know...

21:13.696 --> 21:15.990
has a girlfriend.

21:20.161 --> 21:22.497
-He has a girlfriend?
-Yeah. A girlfriend.

21:22.663 --> 21:24.916
-A homosexual?
-Why would she be homosexual?

21:25.082 --> 21:26.709
Homo sapiens?

21:26.876 --> 21:29.962
So you were asking about her species?
She is a human.

21:30.213 --> 21:33.007
I see. Tokita has a girlfriend!

21:33.174 --> 21:35.593
That's right!

21:36.219 --> 21:39.222
-Let's drink.
-What's wrong all of a sudden?

21:39.388 --> 21:42.350
Darn! Why does he have a girlfriend but not me?

21:42.517 --> 21:44.769
Wow, you're drinking a lot!

21:53.736 --> 21:55.655
Congratulations on getting your license.

21:55.821 --> 21:58.115
You're real divers now.

21:58.282 --> 22:01.702
-Congratulations.
-I'm not sure about her though.

22:01.869 --> 22:05.498
-I'm going to get better!
-That's the right attitude!

22:05.665 --> 22:08.251
All right! We're going to Miyakojima tomorrow!

22:10.711 --> 22:14.090
Let's have a toast first!

22:20.221 --> 22:22.306
It looks like they already did.

22:22.473 --> 22:24.642
He's all better. Good.

22:24.809 --> 22:27.144
Oh, dear. They're so impatient!

22:30.648 --> 22:31.649
A masochist...

22:32.900 --> 22:36.028
DEEP BLUE AL FINE
KAYA MIZUKI

22:44.912 --> 22:50.918
A fairytale whispers
In a fake world

22:51.085 --> 22:56.841
Hiding in the complete darkness

22:57.008 --> 23:02.805
I reach for the forbidden fruit
In my last days

23:02.972 --> 23:09.061
Now I know the meaning of the song about hope

23:09.270 --> 23:14.358
A broken gear will never stop again

23:14.650 --> 23:22.074
Even if I were to lose everything
I'd still want you to know

23:22.241 --> 23:28.289
Trapped in the sky so far away
I'm praying with ripped off wings

23:28.497 --> 23:34.128
Because we span together
The vows of arpeggio

23:34.295 --> 23:40.051
If life sparkles only to the beat
Of the resonating stars

23:40.217 --> 23:43.054
I'll sacrifice everything

23:43.220 --> 23:48.309
Till death do us apart

23:54.565 --> 23:57.109
Thanks, everybody!

24:02.490 --> 24:03.658
Yeah!

24:10.456 --> 24:13.417
Hey, don't act so crazy, freshman.

24:13.626 --> 24:15.795
All right. Let's begin.

24:15.820 --> 24:16.962
NEXT EPISODE
"OTORI"
